Clora T-Shirt Web Application :

    Clora is a full-stack T-shirt e-commerce web application developed as a Spring Boot practice project.
    The main goal of this project was to gain practical experience with the Spring ecosystem, backend development,
    database integration, authentication, payment processing, and MVC architecture.

    The application provides functionality for managing T-shirts, user authentication, shopping-related operations, and payment processing using the Stripe Sandbox environment.

Project Purpose :

    This project was developed to improve my practical knowledge of Spring Boot and modern web application development.

    Through this project, I practiced:

    Building REST APIs with Spring Boot
    Implementing MVC architecture
    Connecting Spring Boot with PostgreSQL
    Using Spring Data JPA for database operations
    Implementing authentication and authorization
    Working with JWT authentication
    Configuring Spring Security
    Integrating Stripe Sandbox payments
    Developing frontend interfaces using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript
    Connecting frontend functionality with backend APIs
    Structuring a project using layered architecture
    Understanding how different components of a web application communicate with each other

Technologies Used :
